  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Income and Employment for Women and Youth in the Dairy Sector in North-east Tanz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dairy production in and around Arusha, Tanzania, has good potential, and demand is growing especially for high value butter, cheese and fruit yoghurt. Twenty womens&apos; dairy groups with nearly 2,000 members are in a strong position to benefit from this, but need alot of help to organise themselves, to brand and distribute their products, collect and process milk regularly, upgrade the factory, and work together to be more efficient. Selling more milk means earning more for their households directly. Promoting a joint venture will add to their negotiation power for inputs like fodder, veterinary services, and transport and to mobilise more back up from Government to help care for their cows</narrative>
  </description>
